<doc node='b5cf0064-6a9b' rev='2'><paragraph id='mttvddjsrgd.0' rev='1' h='8804ba66' heading='1'><text id='.1'>Runbook by language</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.21' rev='2' h='90824be3'><text id='.22'>Each language tab says, for each component, exactly what to change: the version to upgrade to, the file to ship, the variable to set, and how to check it worked. Every change goes through the normal build, package and release; nothing here is applied by hand.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.281' h='a150ce22' heading='2'><text id='.282'>Components</text></paragraph><table id='.292' h='524852bf'><row id='.293' h='0bde0d30'><cell id='.294' h='9bd9770c' header='true'><paragraph id='.295' h='ce54f0e2'><text id='.296'>Component</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.305' h='5cd5454a' header='true'><paragraph id='.306' h='43a7241c'><text id='.307'>Who owns the OS and TLS library</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.338' h='601fe931' header='true'><paragraph id='.339' h='98653dda'><text id='.340'>Where the fix lives</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.359' h='ee05a263'><cell id='.360' h='aef7ca8a'><paragraph id='.361' h='1684230b'><text id='.362'>Lambda, managed runtime (zip)</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.391' h='951369ed'><paragraph id='.392' h='32fd72a0'><text id='.393'>AWS</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.396' h='7d49eaf1'><paragraph id='.397' h='ba9fe771'><text id='.398'>Files in the deployment package under </text><text id='.436'><code>/var/task/pq-tls/</code></text><text id='.453'>; variables in the function's IaC</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.486' h='f1e9d69e'><cell id='.487' h='4f7250dd'><paragraph id='.488' h='cd1b62f3'><text id='.489'>Lambda, container image</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.512' h='f463c457'><paragraph id='.513' h='dfbc43f2'><text id='.514'>You, starting from an AWS base image (</text><text id='.552'><code>public.ecr.aws/lambda/...</code></text><text id='.577'>)</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.578' h='1328891f'><paragraph id='.579' h='65190787'><text id='.580'>Files and </text><text id='.590'><code>ENV</code></text><text id='.593'> in the Dockerfile; function variables override image </text><text id='.647'><code>ENV</code></text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.650' h='5ec03c85'><cell id='.651' h='398a69f1'><paragraph id='.652' h='183520d9'><text id='.653'>Fargate (ECS or EKS)</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.673' h='f9cae1f8'><paragraph id='.674' h='8d58cd30'><text id='.675'>You (the image)</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.690' h='9b3759c8'><paragraph id='.691' h='036863db'><text id='.692'>Base image and Dockerfile; variables in the ECS task definition or pod spec</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.767' h='f31f07a8'><cell id='.768' h='d6ee0d07'><paragraph id='.769' h='86e7efb1'><text id='.770'>ECS or EKS on EC2</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.787' h='99b90dd0'><paragraph id='.788' h='7ae7d236'><text id='.789'>You (the image); the host OS doesn't affect the container's TLS</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.852' h='f68c524c'><paragraph id='.853' h='a6e1d3d0'><text id='.854'>Same as Fargate</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.869' h='d3214eca'><cell id='.870' h='b27713cd'><paragraph id='.871' h='eeccfada'><text id='.872'>EC2 or other hosts (no containers)</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.906' h='b05f8e44'><paragraph id='.907' h='08b04193'><text id='.908'>You</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.911' h='c994d23f'><paragraph id='.912' h='53077734'><text id='.913'>OS packages, crypto policy pushed with SSM State Manager, service unit environment</text></paragraph></cell></row></table><paragraph id='.995' h='558dc215' heading='2'><text id='.996'>Where a variable goes, per component</text></paragraph><table id='.1032' h='d31e1821'><row id='.1033' h='21ab1cec'><cell id='.1034' h='19058f54' header='true'><paragraph id='.1035' h='ce54f0e2'><text id='.1036'>Component</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1045' h='04d8f40b' header='true'><paragraph id='.1046' h='f7e7dfba'><text id='.1047'>How to set </text><text id='.1058'><code>NAME=value</code></text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.1068' h='8c0850fc'><cell id='.1069' h='ce307647'><paragraph id='.1070' h='58f0de23'><text id='.1071'>Lambda (zip or image)</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1092' h='8f582b6d'><paragraph id='.1093' h='b397f503'><text id='.1094'><code>Environment.Variables</code></text><text id='.1115'> in CloudFormation or SAM, </text><text id='.1142'><code>environment</code></text><text id='.1153'> in CDK or Terraform </text><text id='.1174'><code>aws_lambda_function</code></text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.1193' h='11ad6c8b'><cell id='.1194' h='14c701c5'><paragraph id='.1195' h='10d29eff'><text id='.1196'>Lambda image, Fargate, EKS, ECS on EC2</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1234' h='f3939205'><paragraph id='.1235' h='05ee89f9'><text id='.1236'><code>ENV NAME=value</code></text><text id='.1250'> in the Dockerfile, so every deployment of the image carries it</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.1313' h='3a2b5c8e'><cell id='.1314' h='7a839faf'><paragraph id='.1315' h='6d38803b'><text id='.1316'>ECS task (override)</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1335' h='69ecfb7e'><paragraph id='.1336' h='36608dd9'><text id='.1337'><code>containerDefinitions[].environment</code></text><text id='.1371'> in the task definition</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.1394' h='2ec55fff'><cell id='.1395' h='34066041'><paragraph id='.1396' h='ddd5c2a2'><text id='.1397'>EKS pod (override)</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1415' h='c98228cb'><paragraph id='.1416' h='44232ece'><text id='.1417'><code>spec.containers[].env</code></text><text id='.1438'> in the pod or Deployment spec</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.1468' h='eac6dbee'><cell id='.1469' h='6e857acb'><paragraph id='.1470' h='449e238f'><text id='.1471'>EC2 service</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1482' h='bed3607e'><paragraph id='.1483' h='49452a2e'><text id='.1484'><code>Environment=NAME=value</code></text><text id='.1506'> in the systemd unit, rolled out by SSM or the AMI pipeline</text></paragraph></cell></row></table><paragraph id='.1565' h='33db442d' heading='2'><text id='.1566'>Shared files (the pq-tls kit)</text></paragraph><table id='.1595' h='771c5fb3'><row id='.1596' h='f1d4875f'><cell id='.1597' h='1735239c' header='true'><paragraph id='.1598' h='50009ce1'><text id='.1599'>File</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1603' h='2895a423' header='true'><paragraph id='.1604' h='681bf81a'><text id='.1605'>Used by</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1612' h='0a49cd9b' header='true'><paragraph id='.1613' h='d4e8830a'><text id='.1614'>Purpose</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.1621' h='26136844'><cell id='.1622' h='08fe87b7'><paragraph id='.1623' h='b77907cd'><text id='.1624'><code>openssl-pq.cnf</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1638' h='a9e84038'><paragraph id='.1639' h='dcc3fe78'><text id='.1640'>Python and .NET on Amazon Linux 2023</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1676' h='d8ca7fd2'><paragraph id='.1677' h='aca9f659'><text id='.1678'>Loads the AL2023 crypto policy, adds X25519MLKEM768 first</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.1735' h='07ddc0f9'><cell id='.1736' h='b17f115e'><paragraph id='.1737' h='24bd56ad'><text id='.1738'><code>openssl-pq-node.cnf</code></text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1757' h='bbaf18f2'><paragraph id='.1758' h='1ae23f66'><text id='.1759'>Node.js on Lambda</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1776' h='d2b1a3d5'><paragraph id='.1777' h='b80f459f'><text id='.1778'>AWS's Node group list with X25519MLKEM768 added first</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.1831' h='afa492b5'><cell id='.1832' h='4b010e35'><paragraph id='.1833' h='ac623aba'><text id='.1834'><code>pq-tls-agent.jar</code></text><text id='.1850'> plus Bouncy Castle 1.87 jars (</text><text id='.1881'><code>bcprov</code></text><text id='.1887'>, </text><text id='.1889'><code>bctls</code></text><text id='.1894'>, </text><text id='.1896'><code>bcutil</code></text><text id='.1902'>)</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1903' h='7f2748a7'><paragraph id='.1904' h='9d191c15'><text id='.1905'>Java 8 to 21</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.1917' h='43f4a23f'><paragraph id='.1918' h='9ecd3959'><text id='.1919'>Makes Bouncy Castle JSSE the TLS provider and enables the ML-KEM group</text></paragraph></cell></row><row id='.1989' h='49c813a4'><cell id='.1990' h='2fb56780'><paragraph id='.1991' h='772d4a11'><text id='.1992'><code>pyshim/sitecustomize.py</code></text><text id='.2015'> plus pyOpenSSL and cryptography</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2047' h='1596c0a6'><paragraph id='.2048' h='86dc2d29'><text id='.2049'>Python 3.9 to 3.11 on Lambda only</text></paragraph></cell><cell id='.2082' h='4ecc1a48'><paragraph id='.2083' h='cc3be7ba'><text id='.2084'>Routes requests and boto3 through pyOpenSSL's newer OpenSSL</text></paragraph></cell></row></table><paragraph id='.2143' h='6b60cb78'><text id='.2144'>The kit is versioned once and pulled in by the shared build template, so a fix to a file reaches every workload on its next release.</text></paragraph><paragraph id='.2276' h='e92c2ea6' heading='2'><text id='.2277'>Checking a workload</text></paragraph><list id='.2296' h='82265e05' kind='bullet'><listItem id='.2297' h='c29d1963'><paragraph id='.2298' h='5dca47b4'><text id='.2299'><bold>Observed:</bold></text><text id='.2308'> CloudTrail </text><text id='.2320'><code>tlsDetails.keyExchange</code></text><text id='.2342'> for its AWS API calls shows </text><text id='.2371'><code>X25519MLKEM768</code></text><text id='.2385'>, and ELB logs show the same for inbound traffic.</text></paragraph></listItem><listItem id='.2434' h='15f32ffe'><paragraph id='.2435' h='8051be12'><text id='.2436'><bold>Test endpoint:</bold></text><text id='.2450'> a test server that accepts only X25519MLKEM768 (</text><text id='.2499'><code>openssl s_server -groups X25519MLKEM768 -tls1_3</code></text><text id='.2546'> with OpenSSL 3.5) fails any client that isn't PQ. Each tab's verify step uses it.</text></paragraph></listItem></list></doc>
